GeneralsX @build ZH Commander 11/10/2026

Build GameNetworkingSockets for iOS.

GNS 1.6.0's CMake knows Linux, Darwin, FreeBSD, OpenBSD and Windows by
CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME and stops with "Could not identify your target operating
system" for anything else; vcpkg's arm64-ios triplet says iOS. The sources
themselves already know iOS (minbase_identify.h: IsIOS() and IsPosix() from
TargetConditionals.h; platform_sockets.h: poll(), as on macOS), so the CMake
branches add nothing but their existence. The one source file that does not is
tier0/dbg.cpp, whose debugger check ends in #error "HALP" for an Apple target
that is not macOS; there it answers false, as for the Nintendo Switch.

Applied after android-os-check.patch, beside whose Android branches it sits.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -163,6 +163,10 @@
 		# GeneralsX @build Android port 12/07/2026 bionic is Linux-compatible
 		# for everything GNS's POSIX/Linux code paths use (epoll, eventfd, ...)
 		target_compile_definitions(${TGT} PUBLIC LINUX POSIX ANDROID)
+	elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES iOS)
+		# GeneralsX @build ZH Commander 11/10/2026 iOS needs no define: the headers
+		# tell it apart themselves (minbase_identify.h, TargetConditionals.h:
+		# IsIOS(), IsPosix(), and poll() as on macOS in platform_sockets.h).
 	elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES Windows)
 		target_compile_definitions(${TGT} PUBLIC _WINDOWS)
 		if(CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "MSVC")
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -336,6 +336,9 @@
 	elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES Android)
 		# GeneralsX @build Android port 12/07/2026 same as the Linux branch:
 		# nothing platform-specific to link
+	elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES iOS)
+		# GeneralsX @build ZH Commander 11/10/2026 as the Darwin branch:
+		# nothing platform-specific to link
 	elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES Windows)
 		if(CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "MSVC")
 			get_target_property(TARGET_TYPE ${GNS_TARGET} TYPE)
--- a/src/tier0/dbg.cpp
+++ b/src/tier0/dbg.cpp
@@ -119,7 +119,10 @@
 	return (nTracePid != 0);
 #elif IsPlaystation()
 	// NDA material
-#elif IsNintendoSwitch()
+#elif IsNintendoSwitch() || IsIOS() || IsTVOS()
+	// GeneralsX @build ZH Commander 11/10/2026 iOS and tvOS too: only a debugger
+	// hint, and the macOS branch above reads kinfo_proc through headers it does not
+	// include for them.
 	return false;
 #else
 	#error "HALP"
